<title>NETHERLANDS: Delta Lloyd raises Wolters Kluwer to buy.</title>
<headline>Delta Lloyd raises Wolters Kluwer to buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (25/06)</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Wolters Kluwer  publishing    249.00  Delta Lloyd bank</p>
<p>COMMENT: Buy (from Hold) Wolters Kluwer is perhaps one of the most ideal companies to assess as profit growth is very predictable and business is stable. It predicted EPS growth of at least 15 pct for the next few years. The share has in the last few months underperformed the AEX. Prospects for the sector are excellent. Further growth for Wolters Kluwer can be expected both organically and through acquisitions.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     7.06    35.3   28.5   2.48</p>
<p>    1997		  8.25    30.2   24.1   2.90</p>
<p>    1998		  9.55    26.1   20.7   3.35</p>
